{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain","id":1260063,"title":"The straight outta left field villain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-10T20:26:05-07:00","id":1260063,"title":"The straight outta left field villain","content":"Most the games have this. The strix, insatiable, abyss, idigram, the huntsmen. What is the promethean equivalent? Is it the alchemists?<br /> <br /> Admittedly, the tormented seems to be having this show up as the big bad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T20:48:16-07:00","id":1260067,"title":"","content":"Let's see: we've got Pandorans (i.e., what you get when the creation process goes horribly wrong), Sublimati (Pandorans who are intelligent; the regular ones are more like beasts than people), Centimani (Prometheans who have no interest in the Pilgramage, and become unstable as a result), and <i>qashmallim</i> (angel-like beings composed of the Divine Fire that either guide or destroy; the former are often helpful, the latter often troublesome, but neither is wholly good or evil). <br /> <br /> Then there's what <b>Tormented</b> will cover, much of which we already known but a lot of which is yet to be revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T20:52:45-07:00","id":1260068,"title":"","content":"Clarity: The Out-Of-Context Apple-Cart-Upsetter of Mage is the Fallen World, not the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Firestorms are treated Promethean's equivalent. The Qashmallim are probably the second closest concept, but really it's the Pyros as a contaminant and flammable substance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T20:53:33-07:00","id":1260069,"title":"","content":"Rule of thumb-If it features in the Chronicle Name, that's The Thing That Ruins Days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T20:57:12-07:00","id":1260072,"title":"","content":"Can't believe I forgot about the qashmallim. It would make sense for them to be the more &quot;what the hell do we do about these guys&quot; kinda threat/odd ally.<br /> <br /> If im being unclear, which i sure do sound like, i mean most the books have a section focusing on out of context villain, such as the strix and idigram. Other lines have night horrors showcasing them, like the insatiable.<br /> <br /> Promethean on the other hand, being a 2nd edition book, does not have one<br /> <br /> Did not get your posts at first <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>. Hmm, so pyros itself is the out of context problem? I'll admit I did not even think of that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 10-11-2018, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-10T22:02:07-07:00","id":1260076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain?p=1260072#post1260072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't believe I forgot about the qashmallim. It would make sense for them to be the more &quot;what the hell do we do about these guys&quot; kinda threat/odd ally.<br /> <br /> If im being unclear, which i sure do sound like, i mean most the books have a section focusing on out of context villain, such as the strix and idigram. Other lines have night horrors showcasing them, like the insatiable.<br /> <br /> Promethean on the other hand, being a 2nd edition book, does not have one<br /> <br /> Did not get your posts at first <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>. Hmm, so pyros itself is the out of context problem? I'll admit I did not even think of that</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a lot of that is deriving from the fact that Firestorms are the designated Chronicle focus-the absolute destruction that clears up the detrimental effects of built-up Pyros correspondingly ties into the problems of Pyros's presence in the world in it's various forms, particularly when it incarnates the &quot;will&quot; of The Principle.<br /> <br /> When things happen with Pyros, things get screwy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T07:14:31-07:00","id":1260122,"title":"","content":"As Arcane says, Pyros is the big danger in the game, which means you're the out of context enemy. You're a walking bomb, dangerous to anyone you're around, but you need to be around people in order to continue your Pilgrimage. Lesser expressions of danger are the Torment you can fall into, but when you get to firestorms, then you're capable of destroying a swath of land and the people who live there. And, if you stop your Pilgrimage, bad things happen to you.<br /> <br /> Walk the road as quickly as you can, but try not to trip, because you may not be the only one who gets hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T07:24:38-07:00","id":1260124,"title":"","content":"This is a pretty enlightening way to see It. Thanks for elaborating guys!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T11:21:42-07:00","id":1260163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain?p=1260069#post1260069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rule of thumb-If it features in the Chronicle Name, that's The Thing That Ruins Days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah that reminds me, was it ever said what Beast's Chronicle name was? I remember reading a dev's post that they had one though I don't actually remember them saying what it was. My guess Heroes since that was the only major Antagonist in the core book but I'm not sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T12:02:44-07:00","id":1260171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain?p=1260163#post1260163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah that reminds me, was it ever said what Beast's Chronicle name was? I remember reading a dev's post that they had one though I don't actually remember them saying what it was. My guess Heroes since that was the only major Antagonist in the core book but I'm not sure</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast, being a game in it's first run, didn't have Chronicle name. New games don't have those-you'll notice Mummy 1st and Demon didn't have a Chronicle name either. Deviant also doesn't have a Chronicle name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T12:09:36-07:00","id":1260172,"title":"","content":"Demon in particular will also have analysts in the 2nd edition corebook, so it have a lot going for it<br /> <br /> Re reading the the firestorm chapter, promethean is very detailed explaining firestorms now that I think about it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T12:09:36-07:00","id":1260173,"title":"","content":"Demon in particular will also have analysts in the 2nd edition corebook, so it have a lot going for it<br /> <br /> Re reading the the firestorm chapter, promethean is very detailed explaining firestorms now that I think about i<br /> <br /> How do I delete these spam","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 10-11-2018, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T12:50:04-07:00","id":1260175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain?p=1260173#post1260173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do I delete these spam</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindly ask a mod to handle it. You can also flag it as spam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T13:37:00-07:00","id":1260184,"title":"","content":"Frankly, \u201cthe ___ Chronicle\u201d was a dodge around the \u201cno Second Edition\u201d ban that CCP(?) had in place at the time. You'll note that just as soon as Onyx Path was out from under their authority, \u201cBlood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle\u201d suddenly got rebranded as \u201cVampire: the Requiem, Second Edition\u201d. Sure, the Chronicles are a nice thing to have; but they're hardly essential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T13:49:22-07:00","id":1260187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain?p=1260184#post1260184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, \u201cthe ___ Chronicle\u201d was a dodge around the \u201cno Second Edition\u201d ban that CCP(?) had in place at the time. You'll note that just as soon as Onyx Path was out from under their authority, \u201cBlood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle\u201d suddenly got rebranded as \u201cVampire: the Requiem, Second Edition\u201d. Sure, the Chronicles are a nice thing to have; but they're hardly essential.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's also not pretend that it's something that hasn't gone forward since it stopped being a dodge for the Second Edition branding- Hunter, Geist, and Mummy all have Chronicle titles post Second Edition freedom(in the form of the Slasher Chronicles, the Chronicles of the Dead, and the Timeless Chronicles), so it's still very much a part of the design for Second Edition games, even if it's no longer dodging that problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T15:11:27-07:00","id":1260205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain?p=1260171#post1260171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast, being a game in it's first run, didn't have Chronicle name. New games don't have those-you'll notice Mummy 1st and Demon didn't have a Chronicle name either. Deviant also doesn't have a Chronicle name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just basing it over something I read though rereading it I got confused on wrong thing. That is it was a post from Dave saying that Deviant did have Chronicle name and I forgot that and assumed it was Beast. Here's the quote anyway.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1188221-what-chronicle-do-you-think-we-ll-get?p=1189962#post1189962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant does have a Chronicle name, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yeah I took that and assumed that Beast had one as well. Because thinking about it, it not having one would make it weird. Sure you can say Demon doesn't have one also but really it kinda does, it just got released before it did. The God-Machine Chronicle. So really if Deviant does have one then Beast is the only one left in the dust, thus me wondering whether it actually has one one or not. </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-11T16:08:09-07:00","id":1260214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1260063-the-straight-outta-left-field-villain?p=1260205#post1260205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm just basing it over something I read though rereading it I got confused on wrong thing. That is it was a post from Dave saying that Deviant did have Chronicle name and I forgot that and assumed it was Beast. Here's the quote anyway.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> So yeah I took that and assumed that Beast had one as well. Because thinking about it, it not having one would make it weird. Sure you can say Demon doesn't have one also but really it kinda does, it just got released before it did. The God-Machine Chronicle. So really if Deviant does have one then Beast is the only one left in the dust, thus me wondering whether it actually has one one or not. </span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then let's keep it simple: No, Beast never had a chronicle name.<br /> <br /> (Also the God-Machine Chronicle is not a chronicle name for Demon, it's also been explictly stated that Demon never had one, and until the Chronicle Name is explicitly added to the actual information pile, it's about as legit as The Hedge being the Astral Barrier and Beasts not being able to Family Tie Abyssal entities, with all due respect to Dave-but whatever.<br /> <br /> That sounds annoyed. I'm not.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 201